al":44,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:44","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Constitution","content":"4 October 1958 (French Constitution)","ordinal":45,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:45","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Legal system","content":"the laws of France, where applicable, apply","ordinal":46,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:46","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Suffrage","content":"18 years of age; universal","ordinal":47,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:47","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Executive branch","content":"chief of state: President Nicolas SARKOZY (since 16 May 2007); represented by Prefect Jean-Paul KIHL (since 17 January 2005)\n\nhead of government: President of the General Council Said Omar OILI (since 8 April 2004)\n\ncabinet: NA\n\nelections: French president elected by popular vote for a five-year term; prefect appointed by the French president on the advice of the French Ministry of the Interior; president of the General Council elected by the members of the General Council for a six-year term; next election to be held in 2010","ordinal":48,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:48","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Legislative branch","content":"unicameral General Council or Conseil General (19 seats; members are elected by popular vote to serve three-year terms)\n\nelections: last held 21 and 28 March 2004 (next to be held in 2007)\n\nelection results: percent of vote by party - MDM 23.3%, UMP 22.8%, PS 10.2%, MRC 8.9%, FRAP 6.5%, MPM 1.2%, other 27.1%; seats by party - MDM 6, UMP 9, MRC 2, MPM 1, diverse left 1\n\nnote: Mayotte elects one member of the French Senate; elections last held 24 September 2001 (next to be held in September 2007); results - percent of vote by party - NA; seats by party - NA; Mayotte also elects one member to the French National Assembly; elections last held 16 June 2002 (next to be held in 2007); results - percent of vote by party - UMP-RPR 55.1%, UDF 44.9%; seats by party - UMP-RPR 1","ordinal":49,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:49","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Judicial branch","content":"Supreme Court or Tribunal Superieur d'Appel","ordinal":50,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:50","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Political parties and leaders","content":"Democratic Front or FD [Youssouf MOUSSA]; Mahoran Popular Movement or MPM [Ahmed MADI]; Federation of Mahorans or UMP-RPR [Mansour KAMARDINE]; Force of the Rally and the Alliance for Democracy or FRAP; Movement for Department Status Mayotte or MDM [Mouhoutar SALIM]; Renewed Communist Party of Mayotte or MRC [Omar SIMBA]; Socialist Party or PS [Ibrahim ABUBACAR] (local branch of French Parti Socialiste); Union for French Democracy or UDF [Henri JEAN-BAPTISTE]","ordinal":51,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:51","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Political pressure groups and leaders","content":"NA","ordinal":52,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:52","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"International organization participation","content":"UPU","ordinal":53,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:53","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation in the US","content":"none (territorial overseas collectivity of France)","ordinal":54,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:54","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation from the US","content":"none (territorial overseas collectivity of France)","ordinal":55,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:55","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Flag description","content":"unofficial, local flag with the coat of arms of Mayotte centered on a white field, above which the name of the island appears in red capital letters; the main elements of the coat of arms, flanked on either side by a seahorse, appear above a scroll with the motto RA HACHIRI (We are Vigilant); the only official flag is the national flag of France","ordinal":56,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:56","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Economy - overview","content":"Economic activity is based primarily on the agricultural sector, including fishing and livestock raising. Mayotte is not self-sufficient and must import a large portion of its food requirements, mainly from France. The economy and future development of the island are heavily dependent on French financial assistance, an important supplement to GDP. Mayotte's remote location is an obstacle to the development of tourism.","ordinal":57,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:57","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (purchasing power parity)","content":"$953.6 million (2005 est.)","ordinal":58,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:58","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (official exchange rate)","content":"$NA","ordinal":59,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:59","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - real growth rate","content":"NA%","ordinal":60,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:60","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - per capita (PPP)","content":"$4,900 (2005 est.)","ordinal":61,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:61","country":"YT","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - composition by sector","content":"agriculture: NA%\n\nindustry: NA%\n\nservices: NA%","ordinal":62,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/mf.html#field:62","country":"Y